# Staging & releases

## Branches

- **`staging`** — default integration. Day-to-day work merges here first (deploys staging Vercel).
- **Feature branches** — stay there until the user wants them on `staging` (avoids a deploy per commit).
- **`main`** — production (viselle.net). Promote only via staging → main when cutting a release.

Never commit or push to `main` in day-to-day work. If the session is on `main`, stop and tell the user. No force-push to `main`.

## Semver (start at 0.0.1)

When promoting staging → main, bump **one** of: **z** patch (user won’t notice), **y** minor (user notices, no break), **x** major (break / retraining).

Phases: **alpha** (0.x) → **beta** (3-month trials) → **GA** (1.0.0+).

## Release notes

Public page: `/releases`. Source: `CHANGELOG.md` and `src/content/releases.md` — keep in sync when cutting a release.

## Before every staging → main (required)

Do **not** merge or cut a release until all of this passes. Report **command output**, not assumptions.

1. **Tests** — run `npm run test` if that script exists; this repo’s default gate is `npm run build` (`tsc` + Vite). Also run **all unit tests** in Beauty-Backend-API (`npm run test`). Fix failures before continuing.
2. **Database migrations** — in the API repo, compare `supabase/migrations/` on `staging` vs `main`. Apply anything that landed on staging but not yet on **production** (staging DB may already have it). Use the API apply-migration scripts. Never invent ad-hoc schema.
3. Then `npm run cut-release -- --bump patch|minor|major` (Windows: `node scripts/cut-release.mjs --bump=patch`). Preview with `--dry-run`. Bump **both** this repo and Beauty-Backend-API to the same version, merge staging → main, tag `vX.Y.Z`, deploy.

## Environments

Staging frontend must point `VITE_API_BASE_URL` at the **staging API** (separate Supabase from production). Never point staging UI at production API/DB for mutating tests.
